    "result_text": "All 292 tests pass, including the new `Cp18Tests`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field for owner creation. When an owner is created, the response now includes `locality` set to `local` if their city is the single most common city among existing owners at that moment, otherwise `remote`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property (enum `local`/`remote`) to the `Owner` schema, matching the style of the existing computed fields.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `locality` field (`@Column(name = \"locality\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `locality` column to the `owners` table in each dialect (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n4. **`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, added `owner.setLocality(determineLocality(owner.getCity()))` and a `determineLocality` helper. It builds a case-insensitive frequency map of existing owners' cities, finds the max count, and returns `LOCAL` only when there is exactly one city at that max count and it equals the new owner's city; otherwise `REMOTE` (also for null/no-owner/tie cases).\n\nNote on a subtlety I hit: the generated MapStruct mapper converts the model string to the DTO enum via `Enum.valueOf(class, name)`, which requires the enum **name** (`LOCAL`/`REMOTE`), while the JSON output uses the enum's lowercase `@JsonValue` (`local`/`remote`). So the model stores the uppercase name \u2014 exactly like the existing `membershipTier` field \u2014 and the serialized response is the lowercase `local`/`remote` the spec requires.",
